            "result_text": "Perfect! I've created `/app/filter.py`. The script removes JavaScript through three main strategies:\n\n1. **Script tag removal**: Removes all `<script>` tags and their contents (including attributes like `type` or `src`)\n2. **Event handler removal**: Strips all event handler attributes (`onclick`, `onload`, `onerror`, `onmouseover`, etc.) regardless of quote style or value\n3. **JavaScript URL removal**: Removes dangerous `javascript:` URLs from `href`, `src`, and `action` attributes\n\nThe script:\n- Preserves all other HTML structure and content\n- Maintains original formatting and whitespace\n- Handles different quote styles (double, single, or unquoted)\n- Uses case-insensitive matching for HTML attributes\n- Modifies the file in-place as requested\n\nTo test it, you could create a sample HTML file and run:\n```bash\npython /app/filter.py sample.html\n```"
